*> Test of ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK (core/src/content-tables.cob): the block key a block item places when the block has another name than the item.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-ITEM                PIC X(48).
 01 WS-BLOCK               PIC X(112).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "test item placed block: wheat_seeds plant wheat, carrot carrots, redstone the wire" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "wheat_seeds" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "carrot" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "redstone" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "wheat carrots redstone_wire" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "test item placed block: sweet_berries plant the sweet_berry_bush, the seeds the stems, cocoa_beans the cocoa" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "sweet_berries" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "pumpkin_seeds" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "cocoa_beans" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCK) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "sweet_berry_bush pumpkin_stem cocoa" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "test item placed block: any other item names no block" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "apple" TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "ITEM-PLACED-BLOCK" USING WS-ITEM WS-BLOCK
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-BLOCK TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
